  10:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  *  @ingroup per_analog
  11:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** 
  12:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** For now only Normal Mode is supported,
  13:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** Sample and hold mode provides reduced power consumption, but requires a bit more setup.
  14:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  **
  15:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** For now connecting the DAC through other internal peripherals is also not supported.
  16:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  **
  17:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** Since the DAC channels have dedicated pins we don't need to pass in a pin config like with
  18:/Users/jonathanbrown/Documents/dev/aura/lib/Aurora-SDK/libs/libDaisy//src/per/dac.h ****  ** other modules. However, it is still important to not try to use the DAC pins for anything else.
